\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {R.1}{\ignorespaces Plan of the U-shape world, drawn by the generator from the tables that write the world file. Filled rectangles are object footprints coloured by zone; dotted red boxes are the exchange slots the carrier jobs pick from and drop on; coloured polylines are the four carrier routes; dashed green lines are the routes of the four people on foot, a dot at each stop and an open circle at the start; the grey trace is the ground-truth route of \texttt  {dataset_dynamic_nofloortexture_00_000}, which aisles A and B and cross-aisles C and E were placed to keep drivable. The band above the north wall is the dock yard with two docked trailers.\relax }}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:plan-u}{{R.1}{3}{Plan of the U-shape world, drawn by the generator from the tables that write the world file. Filled rectangles are object footprints coloured by zone; dotted red boxes are the exchange slots the carrier jobs pick from and drop on; coloured polylines are the four carrier routes; dashed green lines are the routes of the four people on foot, a dot at each stop and an open circle at the start; the grey trace is the ground-truth route of \repo {dataset_dynamic_nofloortexture_00_000}, which aisles A and B and cross-aisles C and E were placed to keep drivable. The band above the north wall is the dock yard with two docked trailers.\relax }{figure.caption.1}{}}
